<title>PORTUGAL: Credit Lyonnais Portugal H1 net falls.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais Portugal H1 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>January 1 to June 30:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Net 0.152 vs 0.278</p>
<p>Financial margin 2.32 vs 2.92</p>
<p>Deposits 82.44 vs 78.21</p>
<p>Loans 65.03 vs 63.61</p>
<p>Net assets 241.84 vs 304.80</p>
<p>NOTE: Credit Lyonnais Portugal said it did not expect to pay out a dividend on its 1996 results. &quot;We think it advisable to continue with the rigour and transparency pursued by the bank in covering risks and we do not foresee a dividend payment,&quot; it said in a report published in the Lisbon bourse bulletin.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
